l":"harminder01@hotmail.com","name":"harminder01"},{"email":"bkrainer@hubspot.com","name":"bkrainer-hs"},{"email":"hilker.j@gmail.com","name":"jhilker"},{"email":"atanasiuk@hubspot.com","name":"atanasiuk"},{"email":"ksvirkou@hubspot.com","name":"ksvirkou-hubspot"},{"email":"branden@rodgersworld.com","name":"brodgers16"},{"email":"service-ccs+npmjs.com@hubspot.com","name":"service-ccs"},{"email":"evdavis@hubspot.com","name":"evdavis_hubspot"},{"email":"tfinley@hubspot.com","name":"tfinley_hs"},{"email":"jyeager@hubspot.com","name":"jyeager_hubspot"},{"email":"hthakkar@hubspot.com","name":"hemangthakkar"},{"email":"mshannon@hubspot.com","name":"mshannon_hs"},{"email":"psteeleidem@hubspot.com","name":"psteeleidem-hs"},{"email":"amead@hubspot.com","name":"amead_hs"},{"email":"jnorthridge@hubspot.com","name":"jnorthridge_hubspot"},{"email":"eling@hubspot.com","name":"elingyr"},{"email":"tscales@hubspot.com","name":"tscales"},{"email":"rsegura@hubspot.com","name":"rsegura"},{"email":"akuhl@hubspot.com","name":"akuhl-hubspot"},{"email":"jonmiller@hubspot.com","name":"jonmiller_hs"},{"email":"jrosa@hubspot.com","name":"jrosa838"},{"email":"jdye@hubspot.com","name":"joeyd"},{"email":"jedeen@hubspot.com","name":"jedeen-hs"},{"email":"bmatto@hubspot.com","name":"bmatto_hs"},{"email":"bradenmadgett@gmail.com","name":"bmadgett"},{"email":"michaelbrianjean@gmail.com","name":"mjean"},{"email":"bpusey@hubspot.com","name":"bpuseyhs"},{"email":"jevenson@outlook.com","name":"jevenson"},{"email":"krys.danielewicz@gmail.com","name":"userkrys"},{"email":"bvandyck@hubspot.com","name":"bvandyck"},{"email":"jblake@hubspot.com","name":"jblake_hubspot"},{"email":"asliu@hubspot.com","name":"asliu"},{"email":"hweaver@hubspot.com","name":"hweaverhubspot"},{"email":"ankim@hubspot.com","name":"ankim"},{"email":"sebrown@hubspot.com","name":"sehubspot"},{"email":"obreese@hubspot.com","name":"obreese"},{"email":"brwilson@hubspot.com","name":"brwilson"},{"email":"benjaminjbaum@gmail.com","name":"bent0b0x"},{"email":"bash@hubspot.com","name":"bash-hs"},{"email":"ansun@hubspot.com","name":"asun1234"},{"email":"blamattina@hubspot.com","name":"blamattina_hubspot"},{"email":"jazzyclimber@gmail.com","name":"jazzyclimber"},{"email":"jankisgajera@gmail.com","name":"jmcdermott"}],"readme":"# @hubspot/serverless-dev-runtime\n\nA serverless function development runtime that can be used to test CMS serverless functions. This is intended for use with the [HubSpot CLI](https://developers.hubspot.com/docs/cms/developer-reference/local-development-cms-cli).\n\n⚠️ **This is a BETA release that uses some HubSpot features that are not available to all customer accounts. Please refer to the HubSpot [Developer Beta Terms](https://legal.hubspot.com/developerbetaterms)** ⚠️\n\n## Getting started\n\nFor more information on using these tools, see [Local Development Tooling: Getting Started](https://designers.hubspot.com/tutorials/getting-started-with-local-development).\n\n### Usage\n\n#### CLI Command (recommended)\nUsing the CLI to run serverless functions locally, requires installing [@hubspot/cli](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@hubspot/cms-cli). Once installed, to test your functions run…\n\n```bash\nhs functions test <folder.functions>\n```\n\n#### Importing\n\nIt also is possible to use the runtime inside your own tooling. To start the server, the `start` method can be imported from the `@hubspot/serverless-dev-runtime` package and run with settings like so...\n\n```bash\nconst { start } = require('@hubspot/serverless-dev-runtime');\n\nstart({\n  accountId: <portalId/accountId>,                                                  // default: 123456\n  contact: <booleanValueToSpecifyIfContactDataShouldBePassedToServerlessFunction>,  // default: true\n  path: <pathToLocalDotFunctionsFolder>,                                            // required\n  port: <customPortToRunServerOn>                                                   // default: 5432\n});\n```\n\n### Mocked Data\nSome of the data that is passed to the serverless function context is mocked. Specifically the `contact` and `limits` properties. It is possible\nto modify the mocked data by setting values for specific variables within a `.env` file within the `.functions` folder.\n\nThe variables used to modify the data are:\n\n```\nHUBSPOT_LIMITS_TIME_REMAINING       // default: 600000\nHUBSPOT_LIMITS_EXECUTIONS_REMAINING // default: 60\nHUBSPOT_CONTACT_VID                 // default: 123\nHUBSPOT_CONTACT_IS_LOGGED_IN        // default: false\nHUBSPOT_CONTACT_LIST_MEMBERSHIPS    // default: []\n```\n\nUsage example `.env`:\n\n```\nHUBSPOT_LIMITS_TIME_REMAINING=1000\nHUBSPOT_LIMITS_EXECUTIONS_REMAINING=2\nHUBSPOT_CONTACT_VID=456\nHUBSPOT_CONTACT_IS_LOGGED_IN=true\nHUBSPOT_CONTACT_LIST_MEMBERSHIPS=\"some, memberships\"\n```\n","readmeFilename":"README.md"}